Q. What is the arichtecture of kubernetes?
Ans: Kubernetes is a cluster which have mutliple master and nodes. It has mainly divided into two components one is 
"control plane - master"  and other is "data plan - worker". 
1) Control Plane - master
- API Server - API Server is the heart of the kubnernetes. It is the component which is exposed to the external world
where it takes request and acts accordingly. API Server handles authentication, authroization, validation, admission control,
ensuring that only authrorized users and applications can interact with the cluster. 
- Kube-scheduler - Once API Server decides that a pod needs to be installed on a specefic node, scheduler acts on it and it will make
sure that the pod is assigned to that node. 
- etcd - It is distributed, consistent and highly available key-value store that servers as a backbone of kubernetes. It is responsible
for storing all cluster data, including configuration, state and metadata. 
2) Data Plane - worker
- Kubelet : Kubelet is used for creation of Pods and also will make sures that the Pod is always running, if there is any 
issue with the Pod it interacts with "API Server" on Control Plane and retrives Pod specifications and validates them and
later interact with container runtime interface to sotp and start container.  
- Container Runtime: It provides a runtime or execution environment for the Contrainer to run Pods. Kubernetes provides 
options to use any runtime which we like to use like Dockershim, container-d, cri-o etc. 
- Kube Proxy - It is responsible for networking, ip-address, load balancing. 
